// SR 441.1 — Section 5 Preserving and Promoting the Romansh and Italian Languages and Cultures
// generated by src/parse.py. Do not edit by hand.

:NOTE
English is not an official language of the Swiss Confederation. This translation is provided for information purposes only, has no legal force and may not be relied on in legal proceedings.

:INFO
Art. 22 Financial assistance for the cantons of Graubünden and Ticino
1 Within the limits of the authorised credits, the Confederation shall grant the cantons of Graubünden and Ticino financial assistance to support:
a. measures to preserve and promote the Romansh and Italian languages and cultures;
b. organisations and institutions that fulfil supra-regional responsibilities to preserve and promote the Romansh and Italian languages and cultures;
c. publishing activities in Romansh and Italian-speaking Switzerland.
2 In order to preserve and promote the Romansh language, the Confederation may support measures to support the Romansh media.
3 The federal financial assistance shall amount to a maximum of 75 per cent of the overall costs.
|

:NOTE
Art. 22 — Inserted by No I of the FA of 27 Sept. 2024, in force since 1 Jan. 2026 (AS 2025 663; BBl 2024 753).
|

:INFO
Art. 22a Preservation and promotion outside traditional areas of use
1 The Confederation shall support measures to preserve and promote the Romansh and Italian languages outside their traditional areas of use.
2 The Confederation may grant organisations and institutions financial assistance, in particular for:
a. measures and programmes that encourage the learning of the Romansh and Italian languages and the consolidation of language skills;
b. measures and programmes that enable and facilitate the use of the Romansh language.
3 The federal financial assistance shall amount to a maximum of 75 per cent of the overall costs.
|

:NOTE
Art. 22a — Inserted by No I of the FA of 27 Sept. 2024, in force since 1 Jan. 2026 (AS 2025 663; BBl 2024 753).

